<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>X</m> is the number of eggs a hen in Kakamega lays in a week. The table shows its probability distribution.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">0</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">1</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">2</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">3</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">4</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>P(X = x)</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.26}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>p</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>2p</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.14}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) Find <m>p</m>.</p><div><m>p =</m> <fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find <m>P(X \ge 2)</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) Find <m>P(X \lt 2)</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The probabilities of all the values add to 1. The two unknown cells hold <m>p + 2p = 3p</m>, and the other three add to <m>{0.7}</m>, so <m>3p + {0.7} = 1</m>, <m>3p = {0.3}</m> and <m>p = {0.1}</m>. The completed table is</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">0</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">1</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">2</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">3</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">4</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>P(X = x)</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.26}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.1}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.14}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(b) <q>At least 2</q> means 2, 3 or 4: <m>P(X \ge 2) = {0.3} + {0.2} + {0.14} = {0.64}</m>.</p><p>(c) <q>Fewer than 2</q> means 0 or 1: <m>P(X \lt 2) = {0.26} + {0.1} = {0.36}</m>. As a check, this is <m>1 - {0.64}</m>, because every value is either at least 2 or fewer than 2.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{1}{10}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{16}{25}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{9}{25}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>